    "text": "To determine the total number of roses Bella received, we need to break down the problem into smaller steps.\n\n1. Calculate the number of roses from Bella's parents:\n   Bella received 2 dozen roses from her parents. Since 1 dozen equals 12 roses, 2 dozen equals:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 12 = 24 \\text{ roses}\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the number of roses from her dancer friends:\n   Bella received 2 roses from each of her 10 dancer friends. Therefore, the total number of roses from her friends is:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 10 = 20 \\text{ roses}\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the roses from her parents and her friends to find the total number of roses:\n   \\[\n   24 + 20 = 44 \\text{ roses}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of roses Bella received is \\(\\boxed{44}\\).",
